>> Explain, Oh Grand Chief Lojbanistan. I don't quite see the difference. I
>> interpret as "have need of" vs. "am required to" where {nitcu} has some
>> kind of implicit raising.
>>
>
>
> {mi nitcu co klama le zarci mu'i lo nu mi djica lo ladru}
> "I need to go to the store because I want milk."
> In order to satisfy my desire (milk), there is something that must happen
> (go to the store).
>
>
> {mi bilga co klama le zarci mu'i lo nu le mamta cu cpedu}
> "I need to go to the store because my mother asked me to."
> In order to satisfy my obligation (mother's request), there is something
> that must happen (go to the store).
